    "cursorSync": "Off",
    "description": "Super Typhoon In-fa in one ECMWF forecast run: a voxel wherever the air is near saturation, on eleven levels from the sea to 14 km, played over two days with the Time Brush; Mosaic charts of the storm from the side, by height and by side of the eye filter the 3D map.",
    "editable": true,
    "elements": {
      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "id": 1,
          "links": [],
          "title": "What you are looking at",
          "vizConfig": {
            "group": "text",
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "code": {
                  "language": "plaintext",
                  "showLineNumbers": false,
                  "showMiniMap": false
                },
                "content": "Super Typhoon In-fa as the ECMWF model saw it in one forecast run: relative humidity on eleven pressure levels (1000 to 150 hPa, from the sea to some 14 km), and a voxel wherever the air is at least as humid as the threshold above, near saturation, where cloud forms. These are the model’s clouds, not observed ones. Brush a six-hour window or press play: the map shows the forecast valid at the window’s end, the browser holding every step (Chaski), so nothing is asked of the server as it plays. On the right, the storm from the side (distance from the eye against height), how high the humid air goes and which side of the eye it is on: brush any of them and the map, the bars and the other charts keep those voxels. Heights are lifted by the factor above. Tilt and turn the map with the right button or Ctrl+drag. One forecast run (29 October 2026, 18 UTC). Data: [ECMWF Open Data](https://www.ecmwf.int/en/forecasts/datasets/open-data), CC BY 4.0; the red dots are the eye in the model, its lowest sea-level pressure, every six hours.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": "13.2.1"
          }
        }
      },
      "panel-2": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdbwasm"
                      },
                      "group": "ubica-chaski-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "rawSql": "-- A voxel for each cell and pressure level whose humidity reaches the threshold\n-- picked above, at the height of its level in the standard atmosphere, lifted\n-- by the factor picked above. The map shows the step in the window of the brush,\n-- the voxels the charts keep (the cloudFilters selection, on the GPU).\nSELECT time, valid_at, latitude, longitude,\n       44330.8 * (1 - pow(level_hpa / 1013.25, 0.190263)) * ${lift:raw} AS altitude,\n       height_km, height_class, level_hpa, humidity_pct, distance_km, bearing_deg\nFROM $clouds\nWHERE humidity_pct \u003e= ${rh:raw}\n",
                        "refId": "A"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- The storm's eye at each step of the run: the model's lowest sea-level\n-- pressure near its track (datasets/cyclone-clouds/build.sh).\nSELECT strftime(valid_time, '%b %-d %H:%M UTC') AS valid_at,\n       latitude, longitude, msl_hpa AS eye_hpa\nFROM 'http://feeds/datasets/cyclone-clouds/centres.parquet'\nORDER BY valid_time\n"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "B"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Drag with the right button (or Ctrl) to tilt and turn. Each voxel: a 0.25 degree cell and pressure level whose humidity reaches the threshold. The charts on the right filter it.",
